{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['investigations']=d.get('investigations',[])\nd['investigations'].append({\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@recovery\\\",\\\"id\\\":None,\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"When a node's in-memory configuration is empty after a restart with RestoreCommittedLogs, what can an operator actually do: does live bootstrap on the running node repair it, and does the documented RecoverCluster path on the stopped node repair it?\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"cfg_doc\\\"],\n \\\"parent_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"Live bootstrap does not help, because it refuses when the cluster is not new (existing term, log and snapshots), while RecoverCluster does repair the node: it reads the existing state, writes a snapshot carrying the supplied configuration and truncates the log, so the next NewRaft restores that configuration from the snapshot instead of from the skipped log prefix.\\\",\n \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Single-voter cluster bootstrapped, commands committed, node restarted with the flag so its configuration is empty; then (a) call BootstrapCluster on the running node and record the error and the configuration size, and (b) stop the node, run RecoverCluster with the same stores and the original configuration, start it again and record the configuration size and whether it leads.\\\",\n \\\"disposition\\\":\\\"active\\\"})\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@recovery\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_recovery_paths_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"cfg_doc\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-process single-voter cluster at protocol version 3 with 50ms timeouts and RestoreCommittedLogs enabled: bootstrap, become leader, commit five commands, restart on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore with the flag so the configuration is empty (recorded: zero servers, no leader within two seconds, staged commit 6, log last index 7), then attempt live bootstrap on the running node and, after stopping it, RecoverCluster with the original configuration followed by a fresh NewRaft; each step records the outcome and the resulting configuration size.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Live bootstrap and RecoverCluster are the two operator entry points the library documents for (re)establishing a configuration; both are called with the configuration this cluster was originally bootstrapped with.\\\",\\\"RecoverCluster is documented as an explicit, unsafe-by-design disaster-recovery operation, so its success here is a repair capability, not a normal path.\\\",\\\"The stores are the real ones produced by the earlier phases; nothing is fabricated.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No multi-voter scenario: the probe asks whether an operator can repair one node's configuration, which the failing cluster-wide state needs before any election is possible.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"peers\\\":1,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":50}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap, real election, real commits, real graceful shutdown and restart with the flag reproducing the empty configuration, then the two operator entry points called through the public API with the same stores and configuration.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_recovery_live\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"lost_configuration\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"probe\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"operator_recovery_after_lost_configuration\\\"}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_recovery_cc\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"lost_configuration\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"probe\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"operator_recovery_after_lost_configuration\\\"}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"live_bootstrap_attempt\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"probe\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_recovery_live\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Live bootstrap on a node whose state exists must either repair the configuration or, if it refuses, leave the state unchanged; the assertion records whether it repaired it.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"recover_cluster_attempt\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"probe\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_recovery_cc\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The documented disaster-recovery path must restore the supplied configuration on the stopped node, so that the node can lead again.\\\"}\n ]\n}\npar=d['interpretations'][0]\npar['limitations'].append(\\\"Operator recovery in the lost-configuration state is being executed: a construction-time run of a dedicated harness reproduced the empty configuration and then showed live bootstrap refusing with 'bootstrap only works on new clusters' while leaving the configuration empty, and RecoverCluster on the stopped node succeeding (fresh NewRaft with one server that became leader within three seconds). Its retained receipt is requested in this update; together with the existing receipts this makes the repair picture complete: in-protocol via a later configuration entry from a correct leader, operator restart without the flag, or RecoverCluster on a stopped node, but not live bootstrap and not an incoming snapshot for a node with a complete log.\\\")\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
